---
description: Resolve the actual workspace-config goal through semantic composition and exact native authorities.
args:
  goal: string
returns: ConfigResult | null
---
Interpret the requested current configuration finding, comparison or conditional local record. Use the owned workspace brief and current config/history/dependency codebase to choose the relevant questions and evidence. An old workspace name, epoch or saved note is not current configuration authority. Distinguish active settings from working, committed and main declarations, and declared template sources from the running projection.

Compose investigation and semantic disposition according to the actual requested scope. Keep uninspected facts honest instead of inventing a manifest or dependency read. A private record is a separate user-authorized effect: resolve its condition from actual evidence and native feedback. Do not change configuration, deploy or switch workspaces. Return actual requested domain findings and an authentic optional handoff; null represents genuinely unavailable owned evidence, not a claimed successful review.
